(5742437, 834049, 38162, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nuzzer:</b></div><hr/><i> Which country? Oh, if I look close I can see these are US dollars. SO the spirit of the USA is greedy capitialism is it? I''m not convinced. The shot lacks definition. Sorry, DNMC IMO. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>his "statement" is spot on the challenge, IMO.  the greed is good immorality ran into the perfect storm of a willfully ignorant populace that worships militarism.  guess what?  we cant afford empire now.  time to see if perhaps our values are askew; time to see if our citizens might needs some of these bucks instead of the arms merchants and the other war profiteers.  but I digress.  great job of smacking the challenge theme over the head!</td>', 'Originally posted by Nuzzer: Which country? Oh, if I look close I can see these are US dollars. SO the spirit of the USA is greedy capitialism is it? I''m not convinced. The shot lacks definition. Sorry, DNMC IMO.   his "statement" is spot on the challenge, IMO.  the greed is good immorality ran into the perfect storm of a willfully ignorant populace that worships militarism.  guess what?  we cant afford empire now.  time to see if perhaps our values are askew; time to see if our citizens might needs some of these bucks instead of the arms merchants and the other war profiteers.  but I digress.  great job of smacking the challenge theme over the head!', '2009-11-26 01:02:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5742440, 834268, 38162, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dirt_Diver:</b></div><hr/><i> This is an awesome shot but the details say,<br/> <br/>Details:  	Photograph someone or something that can represent the spirit of a country creatively. <i><u>For example, it is a stereotype using an eagle as a symbol of USA. However, challengers could photograph something else to represent the spirit of USA instead of an eagle.</u></i> <br/> <br/>This is a nail bitter. It''s a really crisp shot but the fact that it says don''t photograph an eagle makes me not want to give it a high score. Ughhh I''ll have to vote on the whole challenge and come back to this one. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>so why such a high finish?  guess nobody read the damn rules this time around.  super cliche shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by Dirt_Diver: This is an awesome shot but the details say, Details:  	Photograph someone or something that can represent the spirit of a country creatively. For example, it is a stereotype using an eagle as a symbol of USA. However, challengers could photograph something else to represent the spirit of USA instead of an eagle.  This is a nail bitter. It''s a really crisp shot but the fact that it says don''t photograph an eagle makes me not want to give it a high score. Ughhh I''ll have to vote on the whole challenge and come back to this one.   so why such a high finish?  guess nobody read the damn rules this time around.  super cliche shot.', '2009-11-26 01:08:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5742462, 834285, 18655, '<td valign="top">Perfect! Could easily been an advertisement and it definitely makes me want a shot right now. It also reminds me of 20 years in Canada with nothing but good memories.</td>', 'Perfect! Could easily been an advertisement and it definitely makes me want a shot right now. It also reminds me of 20 years in Canada with nothing but good memories.', '2009-11-26 02:41:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5742509, 834251, 3724, '<td valign="top">Tilt and angle of the cases and glass form an interesting plane..... I see the beginning of a row of archived artifacts in cases artificially illuminated. <br/>I thought originally that these carefully displayed objects contained possibly a series of sewn embroidery of some form. Mundane objects with instant historical value?<br/>Even after your description the objects remain obscure artifacts..... a tee shirt dedicated to firemen, inscribed with sentiment. <br/>The next case is less clear, and the next - only a corner to indicate this continues.<br/>Like the dusty and faded battle flags from another era.</td>', 'Tilt and angle of the cases and glass form an interesting plane..... I see the beginning of a row of archived artifacts in cases artificially illuminated. I thought originally that these carefully displayed objects contained possibly a series of sewn embroidery of some form. Mundane objects with instant historical value?Even after your description the objects remain obscure artifacts..... a tee shirt dedicated to firemen, inscribed with sentiment. The next case is less clear, and the next - only a corner to indicate this continues.Like the dusty and faded battle flags from another era.', '2009-11-26 04:40:41.000000', NULL, 0),
